**Step 4, the MECHANISM PROBE (a node script, no jest, no edit of the repo; written under `session-tools/b713/probe/`).** It requires the clone's `backend/routes/sustainability.js` router and rebuilds the file's `stand` and `hit` by copying lines `:79-102` verbatim (a copy, never an import of the test), then runs, each as its own row with the count, the elapsed time and the first line of every error (classified: `other side closed` / other):
 P0 **instrument control (must fail):** a stand whose server destroys the socket right after the first response, then the next `hit` on the same origin; expect the exact ticket error. If P0 does NOT print `TypeError: fetch failed` / `other side closed` (cause code `UND_ERR_SOCKET`), the instrument cannot see the failure: STOP.
 P1 **shipped shape:** `K` cycles of stand -> 45 sequential `hit`s -> `close`, ephemeral port, defaults, in ONE process (K at least 2000; print how many cycles were handed a port that an EARLIER cycle of the same process had already used: control that the counter works is P2). Also print, for 5 cycles, the number of server `connection` events against 45 requests (expected 1 if the pool reuses one socket; it tells you whether the 45 requests share a socket at all).
 P2 **H2 amplifier:** the stand re-listens on the FIXED port 9800 (then 9801 alternately) for K cycles; the port-reuse counter must equal K minus 1 by construction (control).
 P3 **H1 amplifier:** `server.keepAliveTimeout` set to a few ms and an idle gap of the same order between two requests, and, as the default-timeout row, an idle gap of 6 s once (the only time-expensive row; run it once).
 P4 **H3 amplifier:** P1 while another process of yours keeps one CPU busy for the duration (your own `node -e` spin loop, stopped by pid), only while load1 stays below the limit of STANDING LINE 9 (if it cannot, say so and skip, never run it above the limit).
 Then print the table: row, K, failures, port-reuse count, error class. **Read it: which amplifier reproduces the exact error, at what rate, and does P1 (the shipped shape) reproduce it at all?** Record the result in STATUS under DESIGN as the ranked hypothesis list. Stop the probe's processes by pid and record 9800-9809 free again. The probe runs OUTSIDE the jest lock (it is a single light node process); say so in STATUS.

**Step 5, BASE MEASUREMENT ON THE SHIPPED FILE (jest; the number the ticket asks for).** Everything here runs through the jest lock: `NEXUSAI_LOCK_BASE=/Volumes/Laptop-DEV/'!CODING'/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/locks-laptop-1017 bash /Volumes/Laptop-DEV/'!CODING'/Datasec/NexusAI/session-tools/nexusai-lock.sh jest b713-build-<step> <command>`, `--maxWorkers=2` at most, one ticket per loop (each ticket 40 minutes at most, so the shared lock is not held longer; the loop is one `bash -c` inside the ticket; heartbeat per STANDING LINE 9). Define the units: **a UNIT is one full execution of `driveToCap` (one stand, 45 requests, one close).**
